src/vendor/whg-lpf_v2.0.json: the World Historical Gazetteer's schema for Linked Places Format v2

src/vendor/whg-lpf_v2.0.json is a copy, byte for byte, of the JSON Schema (draft-07) that the World
Historical Gazetteer validates an uploaded Linked Places Format v2 file against, feature by feature:

  repository   whg3, the World Historical Gazetteer's (read from a checkout at ~/Documents/GitHub/whg3)
  file         validation/static/lpf_v2.0.jsonld   (served as https://whgazetteer.org/schema/lpf_v2.0.jsonld, its $id)
  commit       06c9a17e2, on whg3's main (deployed: https://whgazetteer.org/static/lpf_v2.0.jsonld serves it)
  copied       2026-11-18
  sha256       30e27f0d8d55304042fbd51fed5481daa50718df048864f79a98aa73ce5b7f5a

  This copy differs from the one first taken (commit c238ab7e9, sha256 c8cd2c4c...) in two patterns, the
  `lang` definition's and the toponym's, which now admit a private-use tail such as -x-ijmes, and a bare private-use tag (x-ijmes) (the
  schema listed ar-Latn-x-ijmes among its own examples and refused it: WorldHistoricalGazetteer/place#351).

It is named .json here, not .jsonld, only so that it can be imported as JSON; nothing in it is changed
(test/lpf2.test.js holds the copy to the sha256 above). To update it, copy the file again and change the
commit, the date and the sha256 here.

The schema refers to https://whgazetteer.org/schema/csl-citation.json for a collection's own `citation`,
which these tools never write and WHG does not look at when it validates a feature; it is not copied, and
src/formats/whg-lpf-check.js stands an accept-anything schema in its place.

It is used by src/formats/whg-lpf-check.js, to say before a file is uploaded which places WHG would
accept and why it would refuse the others.

